import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — the generic game layer (engine + players + play)","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — the generic game layer (engine + players + play)","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/generic-game-layer.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/generic-game-layer.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/generic-game-layer.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-the-generic-game-layer-engine-players-play" tabindex="-1">Retro — the generic game layer (engine + players + play) <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-the-generic-game-layer-engine-players-play" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — the generic game layer (engine + players + play)”">​</a></h1><p>The codebase had grown three boards and two learned players with duplicated drivers. The productization pass factors the shared shape out:</p><ul><li><p><code>catopt_discovery.engine</code> — the <code>Board</code> protocol (<code>observe() -&gt; state</code> carrying <code>.done</code>, <code>step(action) -&gt; (state, report)</code> carrying <code>.reward</code>/<code>.terminal</code>), the generic <code>run_episode</code>, <code>train_policy</code> (reward-to-go plumbing), and <code>evaluate</code> (paired-board arm comparison). The two arena <code>run_episode</code> functions were already copies; now there is one.</p></li><li><p><code>catopt_discovery.players</code> — <code>LinearPolicy</code>: the softmax-linear REINFORCE learner with the domain injected (<code>legal=</code>, <code>featurizer=</code>, <code>features=</code>). <code>MetaLearnedPlayer</code> survives as a three-line preset binding the meta schema — same tests, same behavior, no fork of the machinery.</p></li><li><p><code>catopt_discovery.play</code> — the registry + CLI. A domain is data: <code>cases</code> (seeded corpus), <code>board_of</code> (case -&gt; Board), <code>legal</code>, <code>featurizer</code>, optional <code>scripted</code> arm. Three shipped:</p><ul><li><code>meta</code> — the meta-arena over <code>meta_player.gen_cases</code>;</li><li><code>joint</code> — forward + derived gradients under one <code>joint</code> root on the meta-arena board (shape-varied archetypes: silu / softmax-spine / linear+tanh — the reverse handler&#39;s programs are board citizens, which is the point);</li><li><code>search</code> — <code>catopt_core.search_env.SearchEnv</code> under the Board contract (<code>SearchBoard</code>): rule-name actions, env reward = normalized cost improvement, horizon/patience terminator;</li><li><code>torch</code> — real <code>nn.Module</code>s (<code>Sequential</code> MLPs at seeded widths) exported via <code>TorchSource</code>, played under the real <code>TorchSink().supported_ops</code> bound: the first product-surface board — scripted pays <strong>+0.23</strong> mean reward on the demo corpus (the sink&#39;s fold laws find real wins, e.g. SiLU folds on <code>Linear→SiLU</code> blocks), where the synthetic boards mostly tie at baseline.</li></ul></li></ul><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>python -m catopt_discovery.play --domain meta|joint|search|torch \\</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    --train-cases N --eval-cases M --budget B</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="what-it-changes" tabindex="-1">What it changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-it-changes" aria-label="Permalink to “What it changes”">​</a></h2><p>Adding a domain used to mean writing a board <em>and</em> a player. Now a domain is a registration entry; the learned arm works on any board whose featurizer exists — verified by driving a toy board through <code>LinearPolicy</code> with a two-feature schema (<code>test_generic_domain_plays</code>).</p><p>The <code>search</code> domain is the honest weak link: rule-fire steps on the current toy corpus find no improvement (all-zero reward table) — the env works, the corpus is thin; richer search corpora are a data problem, not a machinery one.</p><h2 id="where-this-goes" tabindex="-1">Where this goes <a class="header-anchor" href="#where-this-goes" aria-label="Permalink to “Where this goes”">​</a></h2><p>The product claim this sets up: <em>a verified-optimization gym</em>. Every domain is &quot;a program + a legal move set + a referee&quot;; the reward is certified improvement. Next: a <code>Board</code> for the real torch pipeline (<code>TorchSource</code> -&gt; optimize episode -&gt; <code>TorchSink</code> runnable out), which is the user-facing &quot;play my model&quot; surface.</p>`,9)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};